WEBVTT

00:00:01.150 --> 00:00:02.810
<i>I'm Kakeru Aizawa.</i>

00:00:03.430 --> 00:00:06.950
<i>The match to decide the 
school representation</i>

00:00:06.950 --> 00:00:08.650
<i>has finally reached its climax.</i>

00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:11.680
<i>We had struggled for the whole match,</i>

00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:14.240
<i>but with the hotline connected between me</i>

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:16.280
<i>and the returned king, Araki-san,</i>

00:00:16.280 --> 00:00:17.740
<i>we tied up the score.</i>

00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:19.530
<i>It was anyone's game again.</i>

00:00:19.530 --> 00:00:21.870
<i>Then, in overtime after the second half,</i>

00:00:21.870 --> 00:00:24.020
<i>carrying everyone's hopes,</i>

00:00:24.020 --> 00:00:25.830
<i>with my last ounce of strength,</i>

00:00:25.830 --> 00:00:28.420
<i>I sent a final overhead towards the goal.</i>

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:06.000
<b>Conclusion</b>

00:02:06.730 --> 00:02:08.960
The ball is heading 
straight for the goal...

00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:12.770
but Todo blocks it!

00:02:10.580 --> 00:02:12.750
Enoshima Broadcasting Club

00:02:12.770 --> 00:02:15.070
The ball's still in play!

00:02:15.400 --> 00:02:16.530
Will it go in?

00:02:16.860 --> 00:02:17.870
Will it go in?

00:02:18.610 --> 00:02:20.910
Will it go in?!

00:02:23.890 --> 00:02:24.730
<i>Go in!</i>

00:02:29.940 --> 00:02:32.050
Oh, no goal!

00:02:32.050 --> 00:02:34.290
The ball stops just barely 
outside of the line!

00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:39.260
That's the game.

00:02:39.490 --> 00:02:41.370
It's a tie game, 3 to 3.

00:02:41.370 --> 00:02:43.210
Neither team gave an inch.

00:02:43.210 --> 00:02:46.220
They showed us a superb battle today!

00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:48.100
That's was awesome, SC!

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:49.640
Amazing, FC!

00:02:54.710 --> 00:02:56.980
So close, Kakeru.

00:03:05.970 --> 00:03:07.080
Kakeru.

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:09.220
Nice shot!

00:03:09.220 --> 00:03:11.300
I'm sorry. I missed.

00:03:11.300 --> 00:03:12.830
It's fine. It's fine.

00:03:13.180 --> 00:03:15.540
You're really something.

00:03:16.700 --> 00:03:19.550
If you had been playing from the start,

00:03:19.550 --> 00:03:20.970
we would have...

00:03:24.630 --> 00:03:25.600
Araki?

00:03:26.600 --> 00:03:28.320
Hey! What's wrong? Hey!

00:03:28.740 --> 00:03:30.850
Somebody! Somebody, help me!

00:03:31.180 --> 00:03:31.960
Araki-san?

00:03:31.960 --> 00:03:32.810
Araki?

00:03:33.190 --> 00:03:34.940
Get it together, Araki!

00:03:35.340 --> 00:03:36.400
Take him to the doctor's office!

00:03:37.750 --> 00:03:38.990
My st-stomach...

00:03:39.450 --> 00:03:40.440
What's wrong with your stomach?

00:03:41.300 --> 00:03:42.360
I'm...

00:03:42.360 --> 00:03:43.950
hungry...

00:03:52.320 --> 00:03:53.850
Just die there!

00:03:57.640 --> 00:04:00.020
Someone go get him a red bean bun.

00:04:00.020 --> 00:04:01.840
I'll go get it.

00:04:02.880 --> 00:04:05.550
And a ch-chocolate cornet...

00:04:10.730 --> 00:04:14.040
Following the intense game, 
both teams have cooled down,

00:04:14.040 --> 00:04:17.030
but what happens now that 
there's been a draw?

00:04:17.030 --> 00:04:18.680
Will school representation

00:04:18.680 --> 00:04:21.240
be decided by a rematch?

00:04:22.670 --> 00:04:24.310
What is it, Iwaki-kun?

00:04:24.990 --> 00:04:27.490
I have a favor to ask 
of you, Coach Kondo.

00:04:27.820 --> 00:04:28.820
A favor?

00:04:30.310 --> 00:04:34.670
After today, I plan on disbanding 
the Enoshima High FC.

00:04:34.670 --> 00:04:35.560
What?

00:04:36.400 --> 00:04:39.710
I'm asking you, Coach Kondo, 
to take my players

00:04:40.140 --> 00:04:42.300
and bring them onto your SC team.

00:04:43.110 --> 00:04:45.600
They may still be unrefined,

00:04:45.600 --> 00:04:48.010
but they are wonderful 
players full of talent.

00:04:48.340 --> 00:04:51.010
The same is true of the SC eleven.

00:04:53.020 --> 00:04:56.850
Showing splendid effort and leadership,

00:04:56.850 --> 00:04:58.080
Ryoma Oda-kun.

00:04:59.820 --> 00:05:01.370
Entering partway through,

00:05:01.370 --> 00:05:04.030
but scoring through his 
many magic-like plays,

00:05:04.030 --> 00:05:07.100
and claiming multiple assists, 
Ryuichi Araki-kun.

00:05:08.790 --> 00:05:12.230
Physically gifted, making use of 
his height in offensive plays

00:05:12.230 --> 00:05:15.500
and goal scoring ability, 
Michiro Takase-kun.

00:05:16.710 --> 00:05:19.890
Small in build but with splendid 
dribbling and technique,

00:05:19.890 --> 00:05:21.170
Kaoru Matoba-kun.

00:05:22.670 --> 00:05:24.420
The primary attacker,

00:05:24.420 --> 00:05:27.890
and top goal scorer for SC,
 Yuji Sawamura-kun.

00:05:28.310 --> 00:05:29.440
With a wide field of vision,

00:05:29.440 --> 00:05:31.670
and stable ball control and passing,

00:05:31.670 --> 00:05:34.410
pulling through in the first 
half in place of Araki-kun,

00:05:34.410 --> 00:05:35.930
Makoto Hyodo-kun.

00:05:36.340 --> 00:05:39.290
Spectacularly blocking the FC's 
attacks in the second half,

00:05:39.290 --> 00:05:41.610
and also assertively 
participating in offense,

00:05:41.610 --> 00:05:43.200
Go Kaiouji-kun.

00:05:44.110 --> 00:05:44.940
Todo-kun,

00:05:45.410 --> 00:05:46.490
Kurebayashi-kun,

00:05:46.490 --> 00:05:48.240
both keepers with beautiful saves.

00:05:48.660 --> 00:05:50.640
Yakumo-kun's sideline advance,

00:05:50.640 --> 00:05:53.530
and Kota Nakatsuka-kun's 
overlap were both superb.

00:05:55.850 --> 00:05:59.120
And breaking through 
the SC's iron defense,

00:05:59.680 --> 00:06:02.290
putting away two goals, 
the thoroughbred striker,

00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:04.510
Kakeru Aizawa-kun.

00:06:07.350 --> 00:06:11.300
He is apparently <i>the</i> 
Suguru Aizawa-kun's brother.

00:06:12.090 --> 00:06:13.890
Is that true?

00:06:13.890 --> 00:06:14.590
Yes.

00:06:15.840 --> 00:06:18.460
At a school without any 
real achievements,

00:06:18.460 --> 00:06:20.900
a collection of this many fine 
players could be called a miracle.

00:06:22.810 --> 00:06:25.450
If their talent and passion 
could be combined,

00:06:25.450 --> 00:06:27.610
winning the championship 
wouldn't be just a dream.

00:06:28.840 --> 00:06:31.510
Don't you think so, Coach Kondo?

00:06:33.030 --> 00:06:35.520
If we demand that the 
school representative

00:06:35.520 --> 00:06:37.620
be determined by the 
winner of a rematch,

00:06:38.200 --> 00:06:41.330
the talent of that losing 
team is squandered.

00:06:42.610 --> 00:06:47.300
As a coach, I cannot do something 
that would waste their talents.

00:06:48.150 --> 00:06:49.920
So, please.

00:06:49.920 --> 00:06:52.280
Allow them a place at your side.

00:06:54.120 --> 00:06:56.020
This reminds me, Iwaki-kun,

00:06:56.660 --> 00:06:58.930
of when you founded the FC.

00:06:59.590 --> 00:07:01.310
Coach Kondo?

00:07:01.740 --> 00:07:03.300
Because of the division in disposition

00:07:03.300 --> 00:07:05.550
between me, the director, 
and you, the coach,

00:07:05.550 --> 00:07:07.510
the team broke in two.

00:07:08.170 --> 00:07:11.490
Defeated by the mere 15 
players on your team,

00:07:11.490 --> 00:07:15.000
my team, with close to 
60 members, fell apart.

00:07:15.950 --> 00:07:18.770
Then, your team won regionals,

00:07:18.770 --> 00:07:21.140
and went to compete in nationals...

00:07:19.940 --> 00:07:23.860
<b>Enoshima High School</b>

00:07:19.940 --> 00:07:23.860
<b>Mikuni High School</b>

00:07:21.140 --> 00:07:23.860
Coach, that story is...

00:07:24.380 --> 00:07:27.210
If only I had withdrawn at that time,

00:07:27.210 --> 00:07:29.880
Enoshima might have won.

00:07:29.880 --> 00:07:31.140
Right, Iwaki-kun?

00:07:32.980 --> 00:07:35.680
After today, SC is disbanded as well.

00:07:35.680 --> 00:07:36.310
What?

00:07:36.900 --> 00:07:39.130
A new team is born.

00:07:39.130 --> 00:07:42.020
Enoshima High's sole soccer team.

00:07:42.450 --> 00:07:44.980
Coach Kondo?

00:07:45.630 --> 00:07:48.750
You be the director, Iwaki-kun.

00:07:48.750 --> 00:07:51.020
Th-That's... Please wait!

00:07:52.020 --> 00:07:54.190
It's the only way I could atone

00:07:54.190 --> 00:07:58.640
for forcing your genius into a 
worthless leadership position.

00:07:59.570 --> 00:08:01.570
You got me, Iwaki-kun.

00:08:02.570 --> 00:08:04.830
C-Coach.

00:08:05.310 --> 00:08:06.970
Thank you very much.

00:08:06.970 --> 00:08:08.230
Thank you very much.

00:08:10.390 --> 00:08:12.760
Neither SC, nor FC,

00:08:13.500 --> 00:08:16.170
Enoshima High School's 
Soccer Club is born.

00:08:19.360 --> 00:08:21.020
What?

00:08:21.330 --> 00:08:22.980
Of course you'd be bewildered.

00:08:23.940 --> 00:08:27.120
However, this is something 
that has already been decided

00:08:27.120 --> 00:08:29.480
through my discussion with Coach Iwaki.

00:08:29.780 --> 00:08:31.500
S-Seriously?

00:08:31.500 --> 00:08:32.440
It can't be...

00:08:32.440 --> 00:08:35.670
Starting tomorrow, you're 
all on the same team.

00:08:35.670 --> 00:08:37.660
Work to improve yourselves 
and each other,

00:08:37.660 --> 00:08:39.570
and keep aiming higher.

00:08:43.820 --> 00:08:46.000
Your faces say you can't accept it.

00:08:46.310 --> 00:08:47.630
Obviously!

00:08:47.630 --> 00:08:50.880
We want to continue to fight 
at your side, Director Kondo.

00:08:51.800 --> 00:08:53.870
SC's soccer alone could 
take on the nation—

00:08:53.870 --> 00:08:56.390
Then why did you go 
against my instruction?

00:08:57.120 --> 00:08:58.130
Back then,

00:08:59.430 --> 00:09:01.640
watching your fight at 
the end of the game,

00:09:02.390 --> 00:09:04.430
honestly, I was disappointed.

00:09:07.500 --> 00:09:09.730
But, it was splendid.

00:09:09.730 --> 00:09:10.730
What?

00:09:10.980 --> 00:09:13.690
One cannot move just as they are told,

00:09:14.200 --> 00:09:16.360
but must think on their own and act.

00:09:16.770 --> 00:09:19.700
That kind of soccer might 
be necessary now and again.

00:09:20.440 --> 00:09:21.920
Director Kondo...

00:09:22.560 --> 00:09:25.360
You have limitless potential.

00:09:25.740 --> 00:09:27.790
Make use of your experiences 
up until now,

00:09:27.790 --> 00:09:29.630
and aim higher than before.

00:09:29.630 --> 00:09:30.640
That is all.

00:09:30.640 --> 00:09:31.490
Yes!

00:09:35.850 --> 00:09:38.380
It's amazing how it all turned out.

00:09:39.040 --> 00:09:39.790
Yeah.

00:09:39.790 --> 00:09:41.840
To think that, starting 
tomorrow, I'll get to play

00:09:41.840 --> 00:09:44.250
with Oda-san and Takase-kun.

00:09:48.700 --> 00:09:50.310
<i>You must be happy, too, Brother.</i>

00:09:50.310 --> 00:09:51.270
Kakeru.

00:09:53.570 --> 00:09:55.360
All right. Let's get started.

00:09:55.660 --> 00:09:57.530
Are you sure you're okay?

00:09:57.530 --> 00:09:59.110
Aren't you tired from the match?

00:09:59.410 --> 00:10:00.620
I'm fine!

00:10:00.620 --> 00:10:03.580
My body's been restless ever 
since the match ended.

00:10:05.800 --> 00:10:07.000
Me, too.

00:10:08.250 --> 00:10:09.710
All right. Here I go!

00:10:12.710 --> 00:10:14.590
You're shaky after all!

00:10:15.270 --> 00:10:16.550
I'm not done yet!

00:10:27.050 --> 00:10:28.020
Yes?

00:10:30.360 --> 00:10:31.940
That was great.

00:10:31.940 --> 00:10:33.770
Soccer really is fun.

00:10:34.220 --> 00:10:35.450
Yeah.

00:10:37.370 --> 00:10:39.730
You're really good, Seven.

00:10:39.730 --> 00:10:41.780
You kept playing when you 
were in America, right?

00:10:42.830 --> 00:10:44.200
I guess so.

00:10:44.470 --> 00:10:46.440
What kind of team were you on?

00:10:46.440 --> 00:10:47.670
A middle school club?

00:10:47.670 --> 00:10:49.090
Or a youth club?

00:10:49.090 --> 00:10:50.580
Who cares about that stuff?

00:10:50.580 --> 00:10:52.790
Don't say that. Tell me.

00:10:52.790 --> 00:10:54.750
Was it a pretty strong team?

00:10:55.950 --> 00:10:57.350
It's... a... secret!

00:10:58.520 --> 00:11:00.210
So stingy!

00:11:03.240 --> 00:11:04.400
That's mine.

00:11:05.780 --> 00:11:08.350
Hello? What's wrong, Mama?

00:11:14.270 --> 00:11:15.550
I'm home!

00:11:17.010 --> 00:11:18.610
Welcome back.

00:11:18.610 --> 00:11:20.280
This is who I mentioned on the phone...

00:11:20.280 --> 00:11:22.550
Director Goto of Nadeshiko Japan,

00:11:22.550 --> 00:11:24.700
and the captain, Taeko Ishiki-san, right?

00:11:25.790 --> 00:11:28.160
Nice to meet you, Nana Mishima-san.

00:11:28.380 --> 00:11:29.250
Or rather,

00:11:29.840 --> 00:11:31.120
"little witch."

00:11:47.190 --> 00:11:49.220
Well then, once again,

00:11:49.220 --> 00:11:52.310
I, Teppei Iwaki, will be 
taking on the position

00:11:52.310 --> 00:11:55.400
of coach of the Enoshima 
High Soccer Club.

00:11:55.710 --> 00:11:57.150
I look forward to it.

00:11:57.770 --> 00:12:01.700
Henceforth, Coach Kondo 
will act as an advisor.

00:12:02.660 --> 00:12:05.370
The captain will be third year,
 Sawamura-kun.

00:12:05.370 --> 00:12:09.700
The sub-captains will be second year, 
Oda-kun and Hyodo-kun.

00:12:08.510 --> 00:12:09.700
Got it.

00:12:10.120 --> 00:12:14.200
Now, in order to pursue the 
inter-high league as a new team,

00:12:14.200 --> 00:12:16.320
there's something that I would 
like to tell all of you.

00:12:17.250 --> 00:12:19.260
Firstly, to everyone once from FC,

00:12:19.260 --> 00:12:21.910
you were easily able to play in matches

00:12:21.910 --> 00:12:24.030
because we didn't have many members,

00:12:24.030 --> 00:12:25.840
but it won't work that way from now on.

00:12:27.200 --> 00:12:29.200
And to everyone once from SC,

00:12:29.200 --> 00:12:30.820
though your coach has changed

00:12:30.820 --> 00:12:32.480
and I expect things to be bumpy at first,

00:12:32.820 --> 00:12:38.210
changes to strategy and practice 
are an everyday occurrence.

00:12:38.210 --> 00:12:39.940
Remember that and try to keep up.

00:12:40.390 --> 00:12:42.180
With regards to the line-up,

00:12:42.180 --> 00:12:43.900
I plan to remake it from the ground up.

00:12:43.900 --> 00:12:45.660
Even players who didn't have 
a regular position before,

00:12:45.660 --> 00:12:47.870
come to practice with the 
intention of stealing one.

00:12:49.460 --> 00:12:52.080
Now, one last thing.

00:12:53.610 --> 00:12:56.390
Let's have fun playing soccer!

00:12:59.800 --> 00:13:04.970
<i>And so, the Enoshima Soccer 
Club has started anew...</i>

00:13:05.340 --> 00:13:06.210
<i>However...</i>

00:13:07.380 --> 00:13:08.890
Hey, Nakatsuka!

00:13:09.820 --> 00:13:11.710
Why didn't you get that?

00:13:11.710 --> 00:13:14.390
What? Where do you think 
you're kicking it?

00:13:14.390 --> 00:13:16.810
Is your head stuck up your ass?

00:13:17.730 --> 00:13:20.160
You threw an elbow on purpose 
just now, didn't you?

00:13:20.160 --> 00:13:22.230
I told you it was an accident.

00:13:22.620 --> 00:13:25.120
You're pretty sensitive for such 
a tough guy, aren't you?

00:13:23.620 --> 00:13:25.120
Hey! Cut it out!

00:13:25.120 --> 00:13:26.820
Th-That's right!

00:13:29.580 --> 00:13:31.240
Cut the crap, all of you!

00:13:31.240 --> 00:13:33.160
If you're gonna fight, 
do it off the field.

00:13:33.430 --> 00:13:37.770
My, my. I expected things 
like this to happen, but...

00:13:39.570 --> 00:13:40.690
<b>Komura Road</b>

00:13:42.310 --> 00:13:44.630
For a moment, I wasn't 
sure what would happen,

00:13:44.630 --> 00:13:46.530
but Sawamura-san saved the situation.

00:13:46.530 --> 00:13:47.800
That's a captain for you.

00:13:49.440 --> 00:13:50.970
What's wrong, Seven?

00:13:51.700 --> 00:13:52.260
What?

00:13:53.010 --> 00:13:55.900
It seems like you haven't had 
any energy since this morning.

00:13:55.900 --> 00:13:59.310
Th-That's not true. I've got energy!

00:13:59.310 --> 00:14:01.230
Well... if you say so.

00:14:12.270 --> 00:14:14.620
I'd play for Nadeshiko Japan?

00:14:14.620 --> 00:14:18.370
Yes. We'd like to borrow the 
strength of the "little witch."

00:14:18.630 --> 00:14:23.880
B-But I don't have the strength 
to be a full representative.

00:14:24.160 --> 00:14:26.240
What are you talking about, Mishima-kun?

00:14:26.240 --> 00:14:28.380
I've already done my research on you.

00:14:28.670 --> 00:14:30.430
If Nadeshiko had you,

00:14:30.430 --> 00:14:32.660
do you know how much we'd improve?

00:14:32.660 --> 00:14:34.260
Please, I'm begging you.

00:14:34.540 --> 00:14:36.140
Director Goto...

00:14:36.400 --> 00:14:39.860
I understand you're currently 
a manager for a soccer club.

00:14:39.860 --> 00:14:42.110
Is that why you have no confidence?

00:14:42.740 --> 00:14:45.070
That might be true.

00:14:45.310 --> 00:14:48.530
So what then? Don't you like soccer?

00:14:49.730 --> 00:14:51.290
I'm sorry, Ishiki-san.

00:14:51.290 --> 00:14:53.630
I still have something 
that I'm uncertain about.

00:14:53.630 --> 00:14:54.540
So, for now...

00:14:54.910 --> 00:14:57.820
I understand. Let's go, Director.

00:14:57.820 --> 00:14:58.830
What? But...

00:14:58.830 --> 00:15:01.770
She's not the "little witch" anymore.

00:15:02.250 --> 00:15:05.010
It's been a year and a half 
since she left soccer.

00:15:05.430 --> 00:15:06.960
She's just a regular girl now.

00:15:08.200 --> 00:15:10.540
There's no use in holding out 
hope for her anymore.

00:15:11.030 --> 00:15:12.390
Please wait!

00:15:14.240 --> 00:15:16.940
I haven't quit soccer yet.

00:15:16.940 --> 00:15:19.590
If you haven't seriously kicked 
a ball in a year and a half,

00:15:19.590 --> 00:15:20.940
it's the same as quitting.

00:15:22.000 --> 00:15:25.520
As you said, it's natural to have 
doubts when you're young,

00:15:25.520 --> 00:15:28.190
but there are people who keep 
walking even if they're in doubt.

00:15:29.860 --> 00:15:32.470
People like that, even if 
they go down the wrong path

00:15:32.470 --> 00:15:34.300
and have to come back,

00:15:34.300 --> 00:15:37.040
they always reach their goal in the end.

00:15:37.040 --> 00:15:38.900
That's what I believe.

00:15:42.430 --> 00:15:44.900
Beach soccer, beach soccer!

00:15:45.310 --> 00:15:46.640
Are you serious?

00:15:46.640 --> 00:15:49.200
I've never heard of a practice like this.

00:15:49.780 --> 00:15:51.930
Come on, what have you got to lose?

00:15:51.930 --> 00:15:54.050
Try it out. It's surprisingly fun.

00:15:55.850 --> 00:15:57.390
You're all doing it, too!

00:15:57.390 --> 00:15:58.290
Let's go!

00:15:58.290 --> 00:16:00.230
Okay...

00:16:02.160 --> 00:16:03.980
I'm glad you're better.

00:16:04.450 --> 00:16:06.440
It seemed like you were worried 
about something recently.

00:16:06.920 --> 00:16:09.790
I'm fine now. I decided 
I'd turn them down.

00:16:09.790 --> 00:16:10.860
Hmm? What?

00:16:10.860 --> 00:16:13.910
Nothing you need to worry about. 
Now, go, go!

00:16:14.570 --> 00:16:18.570
I see. After simple and 
harsh physical training,

00:16:18.570 --> 00:16:21.370
bringing out beach soccer is 
a truly reasonable choice.

00:16:21.690 --> 00:16:23.330
When people are having fun,

00:16:23.330 --> 00:16:25.330
they don't feel tired.

00:16:25.680 --> 00:16:29.540
Yes. In a place with so much 
rejuvenatory energy,

00:16:29.540 --> 00:16:31.400
the muscles relax

00:16:31.400 --> 00:16:34.760
and you can achieve a safer 
and more effective training.

00:16:35.320 --> 00:16:37.050
The fact that you're 
thinking that much about it

00:16:37.050 --> 00:16:39.240
shows you're really an impressive man.

00:16:39.240 --> 00:16:40.560
Oh, I don't know...

00:16:41.010 --> 00:16:42.440
Mark over there!

00:16:42.940 --> 00:16:44.290
By the way, Hyodo,

00:16:44.290 --> 00:16:46.440
is Araki not coming to practice yet?

00:16:46.660 --> 00:16:48.820
With such a sudden loss in body weight,

00:16:48.820 --> 00:16:50.740
he has virtually no stamina,

00:16:50.740 --> 00:16:52.150
and apparently he's in shock about it.

00:16:52.570 --> 00:16:54.720
So he went and disappeared again.

00:16:54.720 --> 00:16:55.490
Yeah.

00:16:55.930 --> 00:16:58.380
Said he'd get his stamina 
back with some training.

00:16:58.380 --> 00:17:02.180
But I bet he's been dying 
to play some soccer, so—

00:17:02.180 --> 00:17:04.560
Looks like you're at it, guys!

00:17:05.360 --> 00:17:06.750
Looks like he made it.

00:17:07.190 --> 00:17:08.210
Araki-san!

00:17:08.430 --> 00:17:10.170
My bad. My bad.

00:17:10.610 --> 00:17:13.130
Sorry I took so long.

00:17:15.250 --> 00:17:17.880
The king is back!

00:17:21.380 --> 00:17:25.030
Let's go all out at practice today!

00:17:27.820 --> 00:17:29.630
Hey, Araki...

00:17:30.330 --> 00:17:32.130
What's with that gut?

00:17:32.130 --> 00:17:34.020
No! Don't look!

00:17:34.580 --> 00:17:36.310
Don't try to cover it up!

00:17:36.310 --> 00:17:38.570
Didn't you say you were training? Huh?

00:17:38.570 --> 00:17:41.230
Well, I figured the most important thing

00:17:41.230 --> 00:17:44.040
to gain back stamina 
would be to eat, so...

00:17:44.430 --> 00:17:45.350
So?

00:17:45.750 --> 00:17:48.300
I rebounded!

00:17:52.380 --> 00:17:54.880
Die!

00:17:54.110 --> 00:17:55.430
I give up!

00:18:00.320 --> 00:18:01.800
I'll have you tell me

00:18:01.800 --> 00:18:03.350
what you think you're doing.

00:18:03.350 --> 00:18:05.470
Like I said, Mr. Magistrate, sir,

00:18:05.470 --> 00:18:08.310
I never meant to enrich my stomach!

00:18:08.750 --> 00:18:11.000
You already enriched it!

00:18:11.920 --> 00:18:13.780
What a splendid comeback, Mr. Magistrate!

00:18:15.040 --> 00:18:17.240
He's ribbing you, Oda!

00:18:18.070 --> 00:18:19.650
Don't you laugh!

00:18:20.520 --> 00:18:22.740
Director, please say something!

00:18:22.740 --> 00:18:25.140
The inter-high league 
matches are starting soon,

00:18:25.140 --> 00:18:27.050
but with the man who wore number 10,

00:18:27.050 --> 00:18:28.520
even temporarily, in this kind of shape...

00:18:28.520 --> 00:18:30.710
Now, now, don't take it so seriously.

00:18:30.710 --> 00:18:32.050
B-But...

00:18:32.050 --> 00:18:34.560
I can understand why you're upset,

00:18:34.560 --> 00:18:37.180
but, for now, let's resume practice.

00:18:37.180 --> 00:18:37.870
Okay?

00:18:40.470 --> 00:18:42.460
Break up into four teams

00:18:42.460 --> 00:18:44.640
and scrimmage with 20 minute halves.

00:18:44.940 --> 00:18:47.710
All right! Let's go all out!

00:18:47.710 --> 00:18:48.730
You can't talk.

00:18:53.230 --> 00:18:54.980
Are you really going to be all right?

00:18:55.600 --> 00:18:57.660
Will things be okay as they are?

00:18:57.660 --> 00:18:59.430
You're talking about Araki-kun?

00:18:59.430 --> 00:19:02.710
Yeah. He may be a genius, but as it is,

00:19:02.710 --> 00:19:04.830
won't it affect the team's morale?

00:19:05.160 --> 00:19:06.790
I think so, too.

00:19:06.790 --> 00:19:07.890
Don't be so soft

00:19:07.890 --> 00:19:09.790
and be firm where you have to be firm!

00:19:09.790 --> 00:19:11.430
It's all right.

00:19:11.430 --> 00:19:14.500
I think he understands that 
kind of thing quite well.

00:19:15.360 --> 00:19:17.340
Uh, and besides,

00:19:17.340 --> 00:19:18.470
when he looks like that,

00:19:18.470 --> 00:19:21.070
I feel as though the team is 
actually pulling together more.

00:19:23.240 --> 00:19:26.430
Araki-kun's intuition 
really is a cut above.

00:19:26.930 --> 00:19:29.940
It isn't "I have to do something,"

00:19:30.380 --> 00:19:33.110
but the thought that 
"we have to do something"

00:19:33.110 --> 00:19:34.650
which helps the growth of the team—

00:19:34.650 --> 00:19:35.670
You're too soft!

00:19:35.670 --> 00:19:37.030
That's too soft!

00:19:37.340 --> 00:19:41.200
In any case, please leave Araki-san to me.

00:19:43.370 --> 00:19:45.730
I'm so hungry!

00:19:46.330 --> 00:19:48.530
When I get home I'm going 
to drink some juice,

00:19:48.530 --> 00:19:52.120
then eat two or three sweet buns 
and meat buns before dinner...

00:19:52.120 --> 00:19:54.130
<b>Araki</b>

00:19:52.570 --> 00:19:54.130
I'm home!

00:19:55.850 --> 00:19:57.760
This is so tasty!

00:19:57.760 --> 00:19:58.640
Right?

00:19:58.640 --> 00:19:59.490
Hey!

00:19:59.490 --> 00:20:00.820
Oh, hello.

00:20:00.820 --> 00:20:01.970
We're visiting.

00:20:02.250 --> 00:20:04.140
Who's visiting?

00:20:04.140 --> 00:20:05.430
What have you guys been eating...

00:20:07.180 --> 00:20:08.430
That's mine!

00:20:08.430 --> 00:20:09.980
Mom, what is this about?

00:20:10.330 --> 00:20:12.450
Oh, you're home, Ryuichi?

00:20:12.450 --> 00:20:14.060
Your school friends are visiting.

00:20:14.370 --> 00:20:16.180
I can tell by looking!

00:20:16.180 --> 00:20:17.850
Why did you let them in?

00:20:17.850 --> 00:20:19.640
Oh, it's fine.

00:20:20.980 --> 00:20:23.230
What are you guys doing here?

00:20:23.230 --> 00:20:25.400
We came to ask a favor of 
your mother, of course.

00:20:25.400 --> 00:20:26.780
A favor?

00:20:26.780 --> 00:20:29.700
Yes, for the sake of the 
future of the soccer club,

00:20:29.700 --> 00:20:32.410
we asked her to help you diet!

00:20:32.540 --> 00:20:36.420
Wh-What?!

00:20:36.770 --> 00:20:39.880
So, please help us out, Mrs. Araki.

00:20:39.880 --> 00:20:41.980
Yes. Leave it to me.

00:20:41.980 --> 00:20:44.250
Starting tonight, we'll have 
half the dinner, and no snacks.

00:20:44.250 --> 00:20:46.590
And I'll cut his allowance, 
so he can't buy food, either.

00:20:46.590 --> 00:20:47.720
Okay, Ryuichi?

00:20:48.010 --> 00:20:49.400
Of course it's not.

00:20:49.400 --> 00:20:50.560
I'm sorry.

00:20:50.560 --> 00:20:52.690
This is for the sake of 
Senpai and the team.

00:20:53.140 --> 00:20:54.920
Thank you for having us.

00:20:54.920 --> 00:20:55.890
Thanks.

00:20:55.890 --> 00:20:56.900
Wait up!

00:20:57.260 --> 00:21:01.360
How about you worry about 
yourself before others?

00:21:01.850 --> 00:21:03.740
If your ball gets taken away so easily

00:21:03.740 --> 00:21:06.740
in one-on-one, 
you'll never be a forward.

00:21:09.000 --> 00:21:11.720
There's a fatal error in your dribble.

00:21:12.390 --> 00:21:15.110
A forward who can't 
perform one-on-one

00:21:15.110 --> 00:21:17.060
when it counts is never going to make it.

00:21:17.060 --> 00:21:18.400
O-Okay.

00:21:18.400 --> 00:21:19.500
It'll be fine.

00:21:19.770 --> 00:21:20.500
What?

00:21:21.100 --> 00:21:23.580
Kakeru will be able to get past it.

00:21:23.580 --> 00:21:25.530
I'll be there with him, after all.

00:21:25.530 --> 00:21:26.780
Seven...

00:21:27.510 --> 00:21:30.250
It really is as Araki-san says.

00:21:30.250 --> 00:21:32.180
I need to practice more and more.

00:21:32.180 --> 00:21:35.170
But just blindly practicing...

00:21:35.170 --> 00:21:37.330
I guess that's not good enough.

00:21:37.330 --> 00:21:39.150
Oh, now that you mention it...

00:21:39.150 --> 00:21:41.110
Some time ago, my brother had said...

00:21:44.740 --> 00:21:46.240
You got it from me again.

00:21:46.600 --> 00:21:49.620
Do you know why you 
lose the ball, Kakeru?

00:21:49.980 --> 00:21:51.990
It's because you're too good, Brother.

00:21:52.250 --> 00:21:53.700
That's not it.

00:21:53.700 --> 00:21:55.590
Your ball touch intuition

00:21:55.590 --> 00:21:57.980
doesn't actually differ much from mine.

00:21:57.980 --> 00:21:58.880
The problem is...

00:21:58.880 --> 00:22:00.120
Yes? Yes?

00:22:00.700 --> 00:22:01.880
Figure it out yourself.

00:22:01.880 --> 00:22:02.630
What?

00:22:04.790 --> 00:22:06.540
Then I'll give you just one hint.

00:22:06.540 --> 00:22:07.590
Really?

00:22:08.020 --> 00:22:12.520
Figure out why "run with 
the ball" is your weapon.

00:22:12.520 --> 00:22:14.090
That's why in a one-on-one situation

00:22:14.090 --> 00:22:16.060
that becomes your weakness.

00:22:18.310 --> 00:22:21.330
That's what my brother said back then.

00:22:21.890 --> 00:22:24.280
If you're good at running with the ball,

00:22:24.830 --> 00:22:26.140
that means...

00:22:27.370 --> 00:22:30.310
I'm good at concentrating on the ball?

00:22:30.310 --> 00:22:31.430
Right.

00:22:31.430 --> 00:22:34.200
So, the reason why this 
becomes your weakness is...

00:22:33.470 --> 00:22:34.200
Wait!

00:22:34.700 --> 00:22:36.390
I'll figure it out myself!

00:22:41.300 --> 00:22:42.890
Nope, I just don't know.

00:22:44.570 --> 00:22:47.630
For now, let's just try 
what we usually do.

00:22:53.470 --> 00:22:54.060
Stop!

00:22:55.390 --> 00:22:57.240
Kakeru, where were you looking just now?

00:22:57.240 --> 00:22:58.480
Where?

00:23:02.090 --> 00:23:03.260
I see!

00:23:03.260 --> 00:23:04.440
I've got it, Seven!

00:23:06.150 --> 00:23:07.950
I've been looking at the ball too much.

00:23:08.520 --> 00:23:11.370
Especially in a one-on-one situation!

00:23:11.370 --> 00:23:13.150
That's right, Kakeru!

00:23:13.150 --> 00:23:14.200
Totally right!

00:23:15.070 --> 00:23:16.660
So then, that time...

00:23:23.410 --> 00:23:26.430
Right. But once you've noticed it...

00:23:26.430 --> 00:23:27.170
Yeah.

00:23:31.620 --> 00:23:32.640
<i>He looked!</i>

00:23:35.890 --> 00:23:36.560
See?

00:23:38.030 --> 00:23:39.050
Yeah!

00:23:40.790 --> 00:23:43.060
It's good that you've 
found your weakness.

00:23:43.190 --> 00:23:44.710
That's true,

00:23:44.710 --> 00:23:48.030
but it's not so easy to 
just change my habits.

00:23:48.370 --> 00:23:50.600
Just keep practicing until it changes.

00:23:50.600 --> 00:23:52.640
I'll be your opponent again anytime.

00:23:52.640 --> 00:23:55.210
Thank you, but I'll be fine.

00:23:55.210 --> 00:23:55.990
What?

00:23:56.180 --> 00:24:00.120
I won't run away again, like last time.

00:24:00.120 --> 00:24:00.960
Kakeru?

00:24:01.800 --> 00:24:04.170
So, go play soccer.

00:24:04.920 --> 00:24:06.750
I want to see it.

00:24:06.750 --> 00:24:07.880
The sight of you,

00:24:07.880 --> 00:24:09.830
playing an active role on the field,

00:24:09.830 --> 00:24:11.310
like you did back then.

00:24:15.120 --> 00:24:17.630
Oh, but I do want you to join me

00:24:17.630 --> 00:24:19.800
in practice now and then, too.

00:24:20.750 --> 00:24:22.220
Thank you, Kakeru.

00:24:22.220 --> 00:24:23.290
There!

00:24:23.290 --> 00:24:25.620
Wh-What was that all of a sudden?

00:24:25.620 --> 00:24:26.600
Nothing.

00:24:33.050 --> 00:24:38.240
<b>Goshima</b>

00:24:35.550 --> 00:24:37.570
Hello, this is Mishima.

00:24:38.360 --> 00:24:39.640
In the upcoming match,

00:24:39.640 --> 00:24:41.750
please allow me to play.

00:24:45.940 --> 00:25:15.340
<b>Next Episode: Panic at the 
Training Camp?!</b>

00:24:46.480 --> 00:24:49.110
Finally in action, the 
Enoshima Soccer Club

00:24:49.110 --> 00:24:51.510
attends a training camp to work 
toward the inter-high league.

00:24:51.510 --> 00:24:53.770
Kakeru works up a sweat 
at tough practices,

00:24:53.770 --> 00:24:56.910
but as they say, the real 
training starts at night.

00:24:56.910 --> 00:24:59.430
Kakeru faces endless 
temptation and fear

00:24:59.430 --> 00:25:01.200
in the springtime of his youth.

00:25:01.540 --> 00:25:03.980
Nana steps forward and
 joins Nadeshiko Japan

00:25:03.980 --> 00:25:06.690
to face off against the world.

00:25:07.130 --> 00:25:08.730
Next time on 
Knight in the Area,

00:25:08.730 --> 00:25:11.520
episode 9: "Panic
 at the Training Camp?!"

00:25:12.780 --> 00:25:14.870
Kakeru, you pervert!
